==Trivia==
*This is not actually the first group for '''Paradoxum Games''', as it has existed under a different name, [[bark woof]], formally known as [[bark woof|Bark Woof Games]].
**[[bark woof]] as a group worked on a few games, most notable one being an RPG dungeon crawler game. However, this project was never finished and then abandoned, with the group being moved over to '''Paradoxum Games'''.
***'''Paradoxum Games''' would try to create another dungeon crawler game in 2020, though after a few teasers, no new information on it was released, meaning it eventually got cancelled.
**Despite no longer actually being used for anything, the group still exists and can even be joined. There is, however, nothing on it, other than a description stating it has been moved to '''Paradoxum Games''' and a funds t-shirt that costs {{Robux|100,000}}.

===Cancelled Projects===
*'''Paradoxum Games''' has had multiple scrapped projects which were teased or mentioned by the developers, though they ended up being cancelled. There are six known projects.
**An RPG which would contain parkour elements. It was stated to be coming out in 2020.<gallery>
ScrappedFirstRPG.png
Scrapped Parkour RPG - Gameplay
</gallery>
**A real-time strategy game where players defend red cube cores against hordes of enemies using their towers. It would be a spin-off to Tower Defense Simulator.
***Towers like the [[Scout]] would make a return here with some changes, mainly due to towers there having multiple paths.
***Players would be able to build up various structures, like walls or barracks, to help defend the cores. Walls would likely act as a way to slow down enemies, while barracks would possibly be the main method of gaining towers.
***Enemies themselves would be similar to enemies from Tower Defense Simulator, the only confirmed one being the [[Normal]]. Another enemy, Sentient Titan, was teased alongside this game, but later a decision was made to make it part of [[Hardcore Mode|Hardcore]] mode.
****Sentient Titan did not end up in [[Hardcore Mode|Hardcore]] mode despite this, but is present in the game, just unused.
***It would have three currencies: cash, coins, and diamonds. As the cash icon is the same as the Tower Defense Simulator cash around the time, it is fair to assume it would be the currency used during gameplay. Coins and diamonds would likely function similarly to coins and gems.<gallery>
